.TH CSTRING_REPLACE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_replace \- replace every non-overlapping occurrence of needle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

ccol_retval_t cstring_replace(cstr s, const char *needle,
                              const char *replacement);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function replaces every non-overlapping occurrence of needle in s
with replacement. It builds the result in a fresh buffer and swaps that
buffer in, so replacement may contain needle without any risk of an
endless loop. When needle is not found the call succeeds and s does not
change.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s              String to change
needle         Substring to search for (must not be NULL or empty)
replacement    Substitute string (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success              - The replace succeeded, also when needle was
                            not found
ccol_invalid_args         - needle is NULL or empty, or replacement is NULL
ccol_container_full       - The result would overflow a size_t
ccol_not_enough_memory    - The buffer allocation failed
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Matches never overlap, and the search goes from left to right
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_find (3),
.BR cstring_set (3)
